@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components

@*
    ── מרחב הפרויקט — the shared Project Workspace ──────────────────────────

    ONE PAGE SHAPE FOR TWO ROLES. A lecturer and a mentor open a project to
    answer the same questions in the same order, so they get the same
    composition — identity, then the journey, then the work itself, then the
    handful of events that are not already on it. What differs is the CONTENT
    of those sections and which rows can be acted on, and both of those arrive
    as a ProjectWorkspaceView the host built from the endpoints its own role is
    authorised for. This file contains no data access and no role check — the
    host declares its Context and supplies content already scoped to it.

    THE TAB BAR IS GONE, AND SO IS THE EXPANDING ROW. ────────────────────────

    הגשות / בקשות / משימות used to be three tabs of one card. Two consequences,
    both of them the reason this pass exists:

      · A project's state could not be READ. Whichever tab was open, the other
        two categories reported nothing — so "what has been submitted, what is
        open, what is being worked on" took three clicks and a memory of the
        first two answers. They are three separate cards now, all on the page
        at once, each as tall as its own content.

      · A request opened INTO the list. The row grew a large block underneath
        it — dates, reason, attachments, a decision form — while the rows above
        and below carried on as if nothing had happened. Nothing said which
        item you were in, and the surface it opened looked like nothing else in
        the product. A row now opens a real detail surface over the page (the
        host mounts it; see OnWorkRowClick), and the row it came from is marked
        while that surface is up.

    NOT THREE EQUAL TILES. The sections carry different amounts and different
    kinds of thing, so they get different weight: the first takes the page's
    full measure, and the other two share the band beneath it, each hugging its
    own content. Nothing stretches to match anything else.

    AND NOT THREE COMPLETE LISTS. Showing every row a category holds replaced
    one reading problem with another: a project with five deliverables, seven
    requests and nine tasks put twenty-one rows on the page, of which three
    needed anybody to do anything. A section draws what is waiting on this
    viewer, what is late, and up to two recently-handled rows for orientation —
    see PwRowRank. Everything else is one click away behind the section's own
    "לכל…", which is where history belongs: reachable, and not competing.

    A SECTION WITH NOTHING ACTIVE COLLAPSES rather than reserving space. Its
    heading and its summary line are the whole card, because "4 מתוך 5 הוגשו"
    beside the title already says everything a list of five settled rows would
    have said, in one line instead of five.

    VISUAL-LANGUAGE REFERENCE: LecturerTasksPage (המשימות שלי) — MCard panes,
    MSectionHeading, MRow-style rows, MEmptyState, and nothing declared locally
    that a shared primitive already draws.

    NO KPI ROW. The lecturer page this replaces led with six counter cards, and
    every number on them restated a section directly beneath it. The counts that
    earn their place are the ones attached to something you can open: a
    section's own summary line, the stage position, the progress figure in the
    header.

    THE SLOTS. Everything role-specific enters through a RenderFragment rather
    than a flag, so this component never grows a branch per role:

      IdentityActions   the role's own project controls, in the header —
                        add-mentor and Moodle status for a lecturer, the
                        guidance-meeting scheduler for a mentor

    CLICKS RETURN A KEY, NOT AN ENTITY. Every row carries an opaque string the
    host chose, and the callbacks hand it straight back. That is what lets a
    mentor row open a submission review while the same-shaped lecturer row
    opens its own, without this file knowing either exists.
*@

<div class="pw" data-pw-context="@Context.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()">

    @* ── 1. Identity — ONE header, not four clusters ─────────────────────

        Title and status on one line, the project's own sentence under it,
        and then a SINGLE facts line carrying everything else: the type and
        mentor chips, the role's own actions, the team, and how far along
        they are.
    *@
    <header class="pw-head">

        <div class="pw-head-top">
            <h1 class="pw-title">@View.Identity.Title</h1>
            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(View.Identity.StatusText))
            {
                <MStatusBadge Variant="@View.Identity.StatusVariant"
                              Text="@View.Identity.StatusText" />
            }
        </div>

        <p class="pw-sub">@IdentityLine</p>

        <div class="pw-head-facts">

            @* Metadata and the role's own actions — one group. *@
            @if (View.Identity.Meta.Count > 0 || IdentityActions is not null)
            {
                <div class="pw-meta">
                    @foreach (var chip in View.Identity.Meta)
                    {
                        <span class="pw-chip">
                            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(chip.Icon))
                            {
                                <span class="oi @chip.Icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            }
                            @chip.Text
                        </span>
                    }
                    @IdentityActions
                </div>
            }

            @* ── חומרי הפרויקט ────────────────────────────────────────────
                PROJECT-LEVEL materials, and only those: the team's own
                working links (ProjectResources) — the shared folder, the
                spec, the design file, the repository. They are deliberately
                NOT mixed with a submission's files or a request's
                attachments, which belong to one item each and live inside
                that item's own detail surface. Three different things, three
                different homes; this one is the project's, so it lives on
                the project's header and stays there while any item is open.

                Nothing is stored or edited from here — the team owns these
                on their own workspace, and this is a read-only way in. *@
            @if (View.Identity.Materials.Count > 0)
            {
                <div class="pw-materials">
                    <span class="pw-materials-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                        <span class="oi oi-folder"></span>
                    </span>

                    @if (View.Identity.Materials.FirstOrDefault(m => m.IsPrimary) is { } folder)
                    {
                        <a class="pw-material-primary" href="@folder.Url"
                           target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@folder.Label</a>
                        <span class="pw-materials-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    }

                    <button type="button" class="pw-materials-toggle"
                            aria-expanded="@(_materialsOpen ? "true" : "false")"
                            @onclick="ToggleMaterials">
                        חומרי הפרויקט
                        <span class="pw-materials-count">@View.Identity.Materials.Count</span>
                    </button>

                    @if (_materialsOpen)
                    {
                        <div class="pw-materials-pop" role="group" aria-label="חומרי הפרויקט">
                            @foreach (var m in View.Identity.Materials)
                            {
                                <a class="pw-material" href="@m.Url"
                                   target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="@m.Url">
                                    <span class="pw-material-label">@m.Label</span>
                                    <span class="pw-material-host">@HostOf(m.Url)</span>
                                </a>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
            }

            @* The team — a second group on the same line. *@
            @if (View.Identity.Members.Count > 0)
            {
                <div class="pw-members">
                    @foreach (var m in View.Identity.Members)
                    {
                        <span class="pw-member" title="@m">
                            <span class="pw-member-initials" aria-hidden="true">@Initials(m)</span>
                            @ShortName(m)
                        </span>
                    }
                </div>
            }

            @* Progress, inline — the same figure and the same bar, laid on
               the header's line rather than stacked off the end of it. *@
            <div class="pw-progress">
                <span class="pw-progress-pct">@View.Identity.ProgressPct%</span>
                <span class="pw-progress-label">התקדמות אבני הדרך</span>
                <span class="pw-progress-bar">
                    <MProgressBar Value="@View.Identity.ProgressPct"
                                  Size="MProgressBar.ProgressSize.Small"
                                  AccessibleLabel="@($"התקדמות אבני הדרך: {View.Identity.ProgressPct}%")" />
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    @* ── 2. The journey ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <div class="pw-row pw-row-full">
        <section class="pw-pane" aria-labelledby="pw-roadmap-h">
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                <div class="pw-card">
                    <div class="pw-card-head">
                        @*  The same heading anatomy every card on this page
                            uses: title, then a quiet count/summary in the
                            trailing slot. It carried its own `.pw-card-note`
                            here — a second class for the object the section
                            cards call `.pw-sec-summary`. *@
                        <MSectionHeading Text="מסלול אבני הדרך" LabelId="pw-roadmap-h">
                            <Trailing>
                                <span class="pw-sec-summary pw-tone-quiet">@View.StagesSummary</span>
                            </Trailing>
                        </MSectionHeading>
                    </div>

                    @if (View.Stages.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="pw-empty">@View.StagesEmptyText</p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <ol class="pw-stages" style="--pw-stage-count:@View.Stages.Count">
                            @foreach (var stage in View.Stages)
                            {
                                var c = stage;
                                <li class="pw-stage @StageClass(c.State)">
                                    <span class="pw-stage-track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                    <span class="pw-stage-name">
                                        <span class="pw-stage-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                        <span class="pw-stage-text" title="@c.Name">@c.Name</span>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="pw-stage-date">@c.Date</span>
                                </li>
                            }
                        </ol>
                    }
                </div>
            </MCard>
        </section>
    </div>

    @* ── 3. The work — three sections, three cards ────────────────────────

        THE ORDER IS THE ORDER OF THE QUESTIONS, and it never changes with
        the data: what has been submitted, what is open, what is being worked
        on. A section that moved when its counts moved would make the page
        unlearnable.

        THE WEIGHT IS NOT EQUAL, on purpose. The first section takes the
        page's full measure — it carries the most rows and the richest ones
        (a title, a milestone, a deadline, a state and an action). The other
        two share the band beneath it and each ends where its content ends;
        `align-items: start` in the stylesheet is what stops the shorter of
        the pair being padded out to match the taller.
    *@
    @*  ONE WIDE COLUMN AND A RAIL, which is the composition both
        reference screens use. The two categories a supervisor ACTS on —
        deliverables to review and requests to decide — stack in the wide
        column at the reading edge; משימות is supporting information and
        takes the rail, with the activity postscript beneath it.

        The previous arrangement gave הגשות the page's full measure and
        then split בקשות and משימות beneath it, so the most important card
        on the page was also the emptiest: a project with one pending
        review drew one row across 1300px. Width now follows how much a
        card has to say, not what it is called. *@
    <div class="pw-work">

        <div class="pw-work-main">
            @foreach (var sec in MainSections)
            {
                @SectionCard(sec, true)
            }
        </div>

        <div class="pw-work-rail">
            @foreach (var sec in RailSections)
            {
                @SectionCard(sec, false)
            }

    @* ── 4. פעילות אחרונה — a timeline, not a card ────────────────────────

        WHAT IT MAY CONTAIN. Only events that are NOT already legible from
        the three sections above: a submission arriving (who filed it and
        when — the sections state the deliverable's state, never its author),
        a request MOVING after it was filed, a guidance meeting that has
        already happened. "A request was opened" is not one of them: that
        request is a row in בקשות, with its status and its filing date on it,
        two hundred pixels up the page.

        WHAT IT IS. Six lines of small type under a label, at the bottom, in
        no card at all. It used to be a full-width panel with the same
        surface, inset and row rhythm as the work card above it — a piece of
        reference material dressed as one of the page's subjects. When a
        project has nothing unique to report, nothing renders: an empty card
        whose only content is "אין פעילות מתועדת" was chrome around a blank.
    *@
    @if (View.Activity.Count > 0)
    {
        <section class="pw-timeline" aria-labelledby="pw-activity-h">
            <p class="pw-timeline-h" id="pw-activity-h">פעילות אחרונה</p>

            <ol class="pw-timeline-list">
                @foreach (var entry in View.Activity)
                {
                    var v = entry;
                    <li class="pw-timeline-item">
                        @if (v.IsClickable)
                        {
                            <button type="button" class="pw-timeline-row pw-timeline-btn"
                                    @onclick="@(() => OnActivityClick.InvokeAsync(v.Key))"
                                    aria-label="@($"פתיחת {v.Text}")">
                                @ActivityBody(v)
                            </button>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <div class="pw-timeline-row">@ActivityBody(v)</div>
                        }
                    </li>
                }
            </ol>
        </section>
    }
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ProjectWorkspaceView View { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>
    /// Which workspace this is. REQUIRED, and each host passes a literal —
    /// the lecturer route passes <see cref="PwContext.Lecturer"/> and the
    /// mentor route <see cref="PwContext.Mentor"/>, so a dual-role account
    /// gets the workspace it navigated into rather than whichever role a
    /// predicate tested first. See PwContext for why this is not derived from
    /// the role list or from UserModeService.
    ///
    /// <para>The component itself draws the same design either way; the
    /// context is declared here so it is explicit at every call site, and it
    /// surfaces as <c>data-pw-context</c> so which workspace rendered can be
    /// read off the page rather than inferred.</para>
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public PwContext Context { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Header-end actions belonging to one role — add-mentor and the
    /// Moodle control for a lecturer, the meeting scheduler for a mentor.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? IdentityActions { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A work row was activated. The host decides what that opens —
    /// every one of them now opens a detail surface OVER this page rather than
    /// expanding inside the list.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<string> OnWorkRowClick { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<string> OnActivityClick { get; set; }

    // ── חומרי הפרויקט ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private bool _materialsOpen;

    private void ToggleMaterials() => _materialsOpen = !_materialsOpen;

    /// <summary>The link's host, as the one piece of context a bare label
    /// cannot give — "מסמך אפיון" says nothing about whether it opens Docs,
    /// Figma or GitHub.</summary>
    private static string HostOf(string url) =>
        Uri.TryCreate(url, UriKind.Absolute, out var u)
            ? u.Host.StartsWith("www.", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) ? u.Host[4..] : u.Host
            : "";

    // ── Sections ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>The wide column — the categories a reader acts on. Written as
    /// "the first two" rather than as "הגשות and בקשות" so this component still
    /// knows nothing about what a host chose to put where.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PwSection> MainSections => View.Sections.Take(2).ToList();

    /// <summary>The rail — supporting sections, at the narrower measure.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PwSection> RailSections => View.Sections.Skip(2).ToList();

    /// <summary>Which sections have been asked to show everything they hold.
    /// Local, and deliberately not a parameter: it is a reading preference on
    /// one card, not a fact about the project.</summary>
    private readonly HashSet<string> _expanded = new();

    private void ToggleSection(string key)
    {
        if (!_expanded.Remove(key)) _expanded.Add(key);
    }

    private RenderFragment SectionCard(PwSection sec, bool isPrimary) =>@<text>
        <section class="pw-pane @(isPrimary ? "pw-pane-primary" : "") @(sec.WaitingCount > 0 ? "pw-pane-live" : "")"
                 aria-labelledby="@($"pw-sec-{sec.Key}")">
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                <div class="pw-card @(sec.ActiveCount == 0 ? "pw-card-calm" : "")">

                    <div class="pw-card-head">
                        <MSectionHeading Text="@sec.Title" LabelId="@($"pw-sec-{sec.Key}")">
                            <Icon>
                                @*  A shape before the word. Both reference
                                    screens introduce every section with one,
                                    and it is what lets a reader find הגשות on
                                    the page before reading anything. *@
                                <span class="pw-sec-icon"><span class="oi @sec.Icon"></span></span>
                            </Icon>
                            <Trailing>
                                @*  THE ONE PLACE THE SIGNATURE GRADIENT APPEARS
                                    ON THIS PAGE, besides a primary CTA: the
                                    count of things waiting on THIS reader. It
                                    is the page's only "look here", so it has
                                    to mean exactly that. *@
                                @if (sec.WaitingCount > 0)
                                {
                                    <span class="pw-sec-count pw-sec-count-live">@sec.WaitingCount</span>
                                }
                                else if (sec.Rows.Count > 0)
                                {
                                    <span class="pw-sec-count">@sec.Rows.Count</span>
                                }

                                @if (sec.Rows.Count > 0 && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sec.Summary))
                                {
                                    <span class="pw-sec-summary @ToneClass(sec.SummaryTone)">@sec.Summary</span>
                                }
                                @if (sec is { AllHref: { Length: > 0 } href, AllLabel: { Length: > 0 } label })
                                {
                                    <a class="pw-all-link" href="@href">@label</a>
                                }
                            </Trailing>
                        </MSectionHeading>
                    </div>

                    @if (sec.Rows.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="pw-empty">@sec.EmptyText</p>
                    }
                    else if (VisibleRows(sec) is { Count: > 0 } rows)
                    {
                        <div class="pw-rows">
                            @foreach (var row in rows)
                            {
                                var r = row;
                                var quiet = r.Rank is not (PwRowRank.Waiting or PwRowRank.Exception);
                                var cls = "pw-row-item"
                                          + (quiet ? " pw-row-quiet" : "")
                                          + (r == FirstQuiet(rows) ? " pw-row-quiet-start" : "")
                                          + (r.IsOpen ? " pw-row-open" : "");

                                @if (r.IsClickable)
                                {
                                    <button type="button" class="@cls"
                                            @onclick="@(() => OnWorkRowClick.InvokeAsync(r.Key))"
                                            aria-current="@(r.IsOpen ? "true" : null)"
                                            aria-label="@($"פתיחת {r.Title}")">
                                        @RowBody(r)
                                    </button>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <div class="@cls">@RowBody(r)</div>
                                }
                            }
                        </div>
                    }

                    @if (sec.HiddenCount > 0 || !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sec.Note))
                    {
                        <div class="pw-card-foot">
                            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sec.Note))
                            {
                                <span class="pw-card-note">@sec.Note</span>
                            }
                            @if (sec.HiddenCount > 0)
                            {
                                @*  Centred at the card's foot, the way both
                                    reference screens end a capped list. It
                                    reveals everything this section holds, in
                                    place; the queue link in the heading is the
                                    cross-project one. *@
                                <button type="button" class="pw-more"
                                        aria-expanded="@(_expanded.Contains(sec.Key) ? "true" : "false")"
                                        @onclick="@(() => ToggleSection(sec.Key))">
                                    @(_expanded.Contains(sec.Key)
                                        ? "הצגה מצומצמת"
                                        : $"{sec.MoreLabel ?? "הצגת הכל"} · {sec.Rows.Count}")
                                </button>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
            </MCard>
        </section>
    </text>;

    /// <summary>The first non-active row in a drawn list, so the boundary
    /// between "needs you" and "already handled" can be marked with air instead
    /// of a caption. Null when a list is all one or all the other.</summary>
    private static PwWorkRow? FirstQuiet(IReadOnlyList<PwWorkRow> rows) =>
        rows.Any(r => r.Rank is PwRowRank.Waiting or PwRowRank.Exception)
            ? rows.FirstOrDefault(r => r.Rank is not (PwRowRank.Waiting or PwRowRank.Exception))
            : null;

    private IReadOnlyList<PwWorkRow> VisibleRows(PwSection sec) =>
        _expanded.Contains(sec.Key) ? sec.Ordered : sec.Default;

    // ── Row bodies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Written once as fragments because each of them is rendered from two
    // branches — a <button> when the row opens something and a <div> when it
    // does not. Duplicating the markup across those branches is how the
    // clickable and unclickable versions of one row start to look different.

    /// <summary>
    /// TWO LINES, NOT FIVE SLOTS.
    ///
    /// <para>Both reference screens draw a row as a name over a context line,
    /// with one soft pill and a date at the far end. This row used to string
    /// its title, its context, its date, its state and its action across a
    /// single line, which is what made a card of them read as a table: five
    /// columns, ragged, and the title fighting four other things for the eye.
    /// The context line costs no vertical space that the 11px row padding was
    /// not already spending, and it lets the title be the only thing on its
    /// own line.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment RowBody(PwWorkRow r) =>@<text>
        <span class="pw-row-text">
            <span class="pw-row-title" title="@r.Title">@r.Title</span>
            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(r.Meta))
            {
                <span class="pw-row-meta" title="@r.Meta">@r.Meta</span>
            }
        </span>

        <span class="pw-row-end">
            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(r.State))
            {
                <span class="pw-pill @ToneClass(r.StateTone)" title="@r.State">@r.State</span>
            }
            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(r.Trailing))
            {
                <span class="pw-row-due @(r.TrailingLate ? "pw-late" : "")">@r.Trailing</span>
            }
            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(r.ActionLabel))
            {
                <span class="@(r.ActionIsPrimary ? "pw-cta" : "pw-cta-quiet")">@r.ActionLabel</span>
            }
        </span>
    </text>;

    /// <summary>ONE LINE: the sentence takes the reading edge and its actor
    /// and date sit at the other end.</summary>
    private RenderFragment ActivityBody(PwActivityRow v) =>@<text>
        <span class="pw-act-dot @ToneClass(v.Tone)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="pw-act-text" title="@v.Text">@v.Text</span>
        <span class="pw-act-meta">@v.Meta</span>
    </text>;

    // ── Display helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>"צוות אלפא · שלב נוכחי: אפיון" — team and stage on one quiet
    /// line, with either half omitted rather than left dangling beside a
    /// separator.</summary>
    private string IdentityLine
    {
        get
        {
            var parts = new List<string>();
            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(View.Identity.TeamName)) parts.Add(View.Identity.TeamName!);
            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(View.Identity.StageName))
                parts.Add($"שלב נוכחי: {View.Identity.StageName}");
            return string.Join(" · ", parts);
        }
    }

    private static string StageClass(PwStageState s) => s switch
    {
        PwStageState.Late    => "pw-stage-late",
        PwStageState.Current => "pw-stage-current",
        PwStageState.Done    => "pw-stage-done",
        _                    => "pw-stage-future",
    };

    private static string ToneClass(PwTone t) => t switch
    {
        PwTone.Blue   => "pw-tone-blue",
        PwTone.Violet => "pw-tone-violet",
        PwTone.Teal   => "pw-tone-teal",
        PwTone.Late   => "pw-late",
        _             => "pw-tone-quiet",
    };

    private static string Initials(string? text)
    {
        var parts = (text ?? "").Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);
        if (parts.Length == 0) return "?";
        return parts.Length == 1 ? parts[0][..1] : $"{parts[0][..1]}{parts[1][..1]}";
    }

    /// <summary>Members are handed over as a full display string (name, and for
    /// a mentor the contact details in the tooltip). The chip shows the name
    /// only; everything else stays in the title attribute.</summary>
    private static string ShortName(string text)
    {
        var cut = text.IndexOf(" · ", StringComparison.Ordinal);
        return cut < 0 ? text : text[..cut];
    }
}
